{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And you shall speak.</b> The reason He said <b>and you</b> is that he himself must personally attend to the matter, to speak to the wise of heart; and although He said ״וְעָשִׂיתָ בִּגְדֵי״ and so forth, HaShem went back and explained His words, for it is not he who shall make them but rather they shall be made by his word. And lest one understand that the main point is that they be made by Moses' word and there is no need for Moses to speak from his own mouth to the wise of heart, therefore the commandment came and said <b>and you</b> — with your own mouth — <b>shall speak to all</b> and so forth." "And it is precise to say <b>to all</b>, for this is one of the most compelling signs that the matter stems from the perfection of understanding and the willing heart — that he should speak the matters to all of them together. For if the matter came from dejection of soul, he would endeavor to say the matters not in the presence of many, and as long as he could speak his words before one he would not speak before two, for the matter would be a diminution to Moses — as though he were not worthy to minister before the King. Therefore HaShem commanded to make a sign for the matter: ״to all the wise of heart,״ and by this it will be known before the eyes of all that it is a willing soul and a whole heart." "<b>Further,</b> it appears that the reason HaShem said in these five verses three times <b>and you</b> is that He came to grant him greatness in three things, and they are: the dedication of the Tabernacle in its entirety — one; the craftsmanship of the Tabernacle and its vessels and the priestly garments — one; and the service of the House of the Sanctuary — one. And HaShem said to him that he receives reward as though he himself had done everything. Corresponding to the bringing of the dedication of the Tabernacle He said <b>and you shall command</b> and so forth — to you they bring, and that is what He concluded saying <b>and they shall take to you</b>, meaning: I command you to have them bring, and they shall bring to you to make. And corresponding to the craftsmanship of the Tabernacle He said <b>and you shall speak to all the wise of heart</b>, and by this they are none other than your emissaries. And it is precise to say <b>to all</b> so that all the actions that will be done in the Tabernacle will be done through your agency and as though he made them. And corresponding to the service of the House of HaShem He said <b>and you shall bring near to you Aaron</b> and so forth — that he come and serve through your agency, and therefore it is precise to say <b>to you.</b> And according to this reading, HaShem commands Moses concerning every action of the Tabernacle and its craftsmanship and its service directly, for according to the truth he is the one commanded, only that He commanded him that he should command others in his stead."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:34:04.648477367Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}